      "description": "Watch Birmingham vs Brentford highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. The Carabao Cup clash between Birmingham City and Brentford promised to be a high-stakes encounter under the stadium lights. Both sides looked to establish their rhythm early on, knowing that clinical finishing would be the deciding factor in this knockout tie. Early Exchanges and Instant Response On August 25, 2026, Brentford wasted no time in asserting their dominance. Just 6 minutes into the match, Callum Wilson broke the deadlock with a precise right-footed strike from outside the box, assisted by Yehor Yarmoliuk . Birmingham City refused to back down and fought their way back into the game in the 28th minute. Demarai Gray unleashed a brilliant effort from distance following a set-piece situation, beating Hákon Valdimarsson to level the scores at 1-1. Brentford Pull Away The equilibrium was short-lived as the visitors regained control before the break. In the 35th minute, Aaron Hickey found the bottom corner with a left-footed finish to restore Brentford 's lead. The momentum stayed with the Bees , and in the 40th minute, Nathan Collins rose highest to head home a Jaidon Anthony cross, making it 1-3. Birmingham tried to respond through Gray and Luis Vázquez , but they couldn't find a way past the organized away defense. Second Half Dominance The second period saw Brentford turn a comfortable lead into a comprehensive rout. After a flurry of substitutions, the goals continued to flow. Mikkel Damsgaard added a fourth in the 70th minute following a lightning-fast break, once again assisted by Jaidon Anthony . Minutes later, Igor Thiago made it 1-5 from close range. The final blow arrived in the 77th minute when Nathan Collins secured his second header of the night from a corner, sealing a emphatic 1-6 victory for the top-flight side."
